        "id": "v2-481a5-p20-practice-slot-9-slot-9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the equation of the perpendicular bisector of the line segment joining $(-2,5)$ with $(4,1)$ in general form.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3x-2y+3=0$. Midpoint $(1,3)$; perpendicular gradient $\\frac32$.",
          "worked": "The perpendicular bisector passes through the midpoint.\n$$\\begin{align*}M&=\\left(\\frac{-2+4}{2},\\frac{5+1}{2}\\right)\\\\&=(1,3)\\\\m&=\\frac{1-5}{4-(-2)}\\\\&=-\\frac23\\\\m_{\\mathrm{perp}}&=\\frac32\\end{align*}$$\nUsing point–gradient form:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-3&=\\frac32(x-1)\\\\2y-6&=3x-3\\\\3x-2y+3&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-481a5-p20-practice-slot-9-slot-9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find where this bisector cuts the $y$-axis.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(0,\\frac32\\right)$",
          "worked": "On the $y$-axis, $x=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3(0)-2y+3&=0\\\\-2y&=-3\\\\y&=\\frac32\\end{align*}$$\nThe bisector cuts the $y$-axis at $\\left(0,\\frac32\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
